WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.030 --> 00:00:02.030
Hey, this is Presh Talwalkar

00:00:02.530 --> 00:00:05.100
Baseball is a game of traditions and rules.

00:00:05.859 --> 00:00:08.729
Rule 2.02 two of the MLB handbook

00:00:09.400 --> 00:00:14.549
carefully defines home plate by the following geometric construction.

00:00:15.219 --> 00:00:18.059
The home base is defined as a square

00:00:18.699 --> 00:00:21.059
where one side is 17 inches.

00:00:22.000 --> 00:00:24.000
Two corners are removed.

00:00:24.550 --> 00:00:30.630
The two adjacent sides measure 8 and 1/2 inches and the remaining two sides

00:00:31.000 --> 00:00:34.559
measure 12 inches and meet at a right angle.

00:00:37.329 --> 00:00:42.749
There's only one problem with this very carefully defined construction

00:00:43.899 --> 00:00:46.619
It's an impossible shape mathematically.

00:00:49.090 --> 00:00:53.489
This creates an interesting geometric little puzzle.

00:00:54.520 --> 00:00:59.249
If we were to say the dimensions of 17 inches and

00:00:59.649 --> 00:01:04.618
8 and 1/2 inches as well as the following right angles are correct,

00:01:05.920 --> 00:01:09.570
what would be the correct measure of the remaining sides?

00:01:10.479 --> 00:01:12.189
That is,

00:01:12.189 --> 00:01:19.300
can you solve for the correct value of x to make home-plate geometrically possible?

00:01:20.440 --> 00:01:26.760
Can you figure it out? Give this problem a try and when you're ready to keep watching the video for the solution.

00:01:33.759 --> 00:01:36.449
So how can we solve for the correct value of x?

00:01:38.710 --> 00:01:41.489
Will divide the shape into two different shapes.

00:01:41.880 --> 00:01:46.240
We'll draw a line connecting the two sides of 8 and 1/2 inches.

00:01:46.440 --> 00:01:50.720
This creates an upper rectangle and a lower isosceles right triangle.

00:01:52.740 --> 00:01:58.280
Because the upper shape is a rectangle we know that this length will be 17 inches.

00:02:00.310 --> 00:02:03.600
Now we can focus on the isosceles right triangle.

00:02:05.079 --> 00:02:10.949
By the Pythagorean theorem x squared plus x squared is equal to 17 squared.

00:02:12.040 --> 00:02:15.900
This means 2x squared is equal to 17 squared,

00:02:15.940 --> 00:02:19.840
which means x squared is equal to 17 squared divided by 2.

00:02:19.840 --> 00:02:25.440
And so x is equal to 17 divided by the square root of 2,

00:02:25.880 --> 00:02:34.380
which is approximately 12.02, which is slightly larger than the 12 inches that's defined in the handbook.

00:02:36.500 --> 00:02:39.260
If MLB wanted to be mathematically correct,

00:02:39.269 --> 00:02:46.919
it could say in the next iteration of its handbook that the two remaining sides should measure about 12 inches.

00:02:47.880 --> 00:02:49.880
Did you figure it out?

